# Redoubt no-build-metadata.patch (LW-M6-02)
#
# Upstream file: mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/
#                org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt
#
# WHAT UPSTREAM DOES
# ------------------
# configureBuildMetadata() registers WriteBuildMetadata for every minified
# application variant. That task reads the `# pg_map_hash: SHA-256 ...` line
# from the R8 mapping header and packages it, plus a UUID derived from it, as
# assets/build-metadata.properties. Mozilla uses it to match crash reports and
# profiles to the right mapping file.
#
# WHY REDOUBT DROPS IT
# --------------------
# It is the only thing that kept the 161.0-1 APKs from being byte-identical
# across machines. Measured 2026-11-26 (release run 45650986628 on runner 24
# vs a fresh-image build on a second VM, both commit 683c8915): every APK entry
# matched except this asset. The two mapping.txt files have the same size and
# are identical once sorted line by line; only the order of the per-file blocks
# in R8's `ComposeStackTrace -> $$compose:` section differs. Every R8 input
# (49,938 class/jar/dex/source files, both Gradle module caches) hashed the
# same. So the dex code is deterministic, but R8's mapping order depends on
# the machine (it is stable across builds on each of the two machines; the
# deciding property is unknown), and this task copies the hash of that order
# into the APK. With this patch, CI run 45953992693 and a second-machine build
# of ba2a9c3b gave byte-identical APKs (2026-11-27).
# Evidence: docs/android/evidence/lw-m6-02/cross-machine-161.0-1/.
#
# Nothing in Redoubt reads the asset: no-crashreporter.patch removes the only
# consumers (Sentry/Socorro) and keeps Analytics.buildMetadata unread, and
# android-components' BuildMetadata.fromAssets() returns empty metadata when
# the asset is missing (IOException path), as it already does for non-minified
# builds. Redoubt does not upload mappings.
#
# The whole function goes, not just the call: the conventions plugin compiles
# with allWarningsAsErrors. Its SingleArtifact import had no other user.
# WriteBuildMetadata.kt is left in place, unreferenced. No other listed patch
# touches this file.
#
# Rebase check: if upstream starts hashing a sorted mapping, or R8 writes the
# $$compose section in a machine-independent order, this patch can be dropped; build twice on
# different machines and compare assets/build-metadata.properties.

--- a/mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt
